---
import BaseLayout from '../../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="SME Funds | Category I AIF | Platizio Alternatives" currentPage="knowledge/aif">

<div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-6 md:px-10 lg:px-12 pb-24">

  <!-- Breadcrumb -->
  <nav class="py-6 flex items-center gap-2 text-[11px] uppercase tracking-widest font-bold text-outline border-b border-outline-variant/20 flex-wrap">
    <a href="/knowledge/aif" class="hover:text-secondary transition-colors">AIF Knowledge</a>
    <span class="material-symbols-outlined text-sm text-outline-variant">chevron_right</span>
    <a href="/knowledge/aif/category-i" class="hover:text-secondary transition-colors">Category I AIF</a>
    <span class="material-symbols-outlined text-sm text-outline-variant">chevron_right</span>
    <span class="text-on-surface-variant">SME Funds</span>
  </nav>

  <!-- Hero -->
  <section class="py-14 md:py-20 border-b border-outline-variant/20 mb-16">
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-12 gap-10 items-end">
      <div class="md:col-span-8">
        <span class="text-[10px] uppercase tracking-[0.3em] text-secondary font-bold mb-3 block">Category I AIF · SEBI AIF Regulations, 2012</span>
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-4 flex-wrap">
          <span class="text-[10px] px-3 py-1.5 bg-tertiary-fixed text-on-tertiary-fixed uppercase font-bold tracking-widest">Category I</span>
          <span class="text-[10px] px-3 py-1.5 bg-surface-container text-secondary border border-outline-variant/30 uppercase font-bold tracking-widest">SME</span>
        </div>
        <h1 class="text-5xl md:text-7xl font-headline text-primary-container leading-tight mb-6">
          SME <span class="italic font-light">Funds</span>
        </h1>
        <p class="text-on-surface-variant text-lg leading-relaxed max-w-2xl">
          SME Funds are Category I AIFs that provide growth equity and structured capital to Small and Medium Enterprises — India's backbone of employment and GDP — at the stage where traditional bank credit is constrained and public markets are inaccessible.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="md:col-span-4">
        <div class="bg-tertiary-fixed p-8">
          <span class="text-[10px] uppercase font-bold tracking-widest text-on-tertiary-fixed/70 block mb-4">Target Profile</span>
          <ul class="space-y-3">
            {[
              'Revenue: ₹10 Cr – ₹500 Cr',
              'Profitable or near-profitable operations',
              'Proven business model with growth runway',
              'Family-owned or founder-led businesses',
              'Manufacturing, services, or export-oriented',
            ].map(item => (
              <li class="text-sm text-on-tertiary-fixed font-medium flex items-start gap-2">
                <span class="material-symbols-outlined text-[14px] mt-0.5 shrink-0">check_circle</span>{item}
              </li>
            ))}
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Definition -->
  <section class="mb-16 grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-12 gap-10">
    <div class="md:col-span-5 bg-surface-container-low p-10">
      <h2 class="font-headline text-3xl text-primary-container mb-6">SEBI Definition</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-on-surface-variant leading-loose">
        Under Regulation 3(4)(a) of the SEBI (AIF) Regulations, 2012, SME Funds are a Category I AIF sub-category that invests in small and medium enterprises — entities the Government of India classifies as SMEs under the MSMED Act. SEBI recognises these funds as socially and economically desirable, given MSMEs' role in employment and export generation.
      </p>
      <div class="mt-8 pt-8 border-t border-outline-variant/30">
        <span class="text-[10px] font-bold tracking-widest uppercase text-outline">Governing Regulation</span>
        <p class="font-headline text-lg text-primary-container mt-1">SEBI AIF Regs, 2012 – Reg 3(4)(a)</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="md:col-span-7">
      <h2 class="font-headline text-3xl text-primary-container mb-6">Bridging India's MSME Credit Gap</h2>
      <p class="text-base text-on-surface-variant leading-relaxed mb-5">
        India has over 6.3 crore MSMEs contributing ~30% of GDP and employing over 11 crore people. Yet the formal credit gap for MSMEs exceeds ₹25 lakh crore — a gap that neither banks (constrained by collateral norms) nor venture capital (requiring high-growth profiles) can fully address. SME Funds fill this void by providing patient equity and quasi-equity capital to established but underfinanced businesses.
      </p>
      <p class="text-base text-on-surface-variant leading-relaxed">
        Many SME fund investees are family-owned businesses with 10–30 years of operation that need capital for capacity expansion, technology adoption, export market entry, or working capital to fulfil large orders. The fund manager typically takes a minority stake, supports governance improvement, and exits via an IPO on the BSE SME / NSE Emerge platform or via a strategic sale.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Investment Approach -->
  <section class="mb-16">
    <h2 class="font-headline text-4xl text-primary-container mb-2">Investment Approach</h2>
    <div class="w-12 h-1 bg-tertiary-fixed mb-10"></div>
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-4">
      {[
        { icon: 'store', title: 'Equity & Quasi-Equity', desc: 'Primary instruments include minority equity stakes, Compulsory Convertible Debentures (CCDs), and Optionally Convertible Preference Shares (OCPS). Ticket sizes typically range from ₹2 Cr to ₹20 Cr per deal.' },
        { icon: 'trending_up', title: 'Growth Capital Deployment', desc: 'Capital deployed for capacity expansion (new plant/machinery), geographic expansion, working capital for large order fulfilment, and selective acquisitions of smaller competitors.' },
        { icon: 'account_balance', title: 'Governance Enhancement', desc: 'Fund managers introduce independent directors, formalise financial reporting, implement ERP systems, and strengthen HR policies — improving institutional quality ahead of exit.' },
        { icon: 'public', title: 'SME Platform Listing', desc: 'BSE SME and NSE Emerge platforms provide a structured exit pathway for investees with turnover of ₹5 Cr – ₹300 Cr. Over 600 companies have listed on SME platforms since inception.' },
        { icon: 'handshake', title: 'Strategic Sale', desc: 'Large corporates, PE funds, and MNCs seeking market entry or inorganic growth in India frequently acquire SME investees at 3–5× revenue multiples, providing a clean exit to the fund.' },
        { icon: 'workspace_premium', title: 'Sector Focus', desc: 'Leading SME AIF managers focus on specific sectors: specialty chemicals, auto ancillaries, pharma API, food processing, technical textiles, and B2B SaaS — where local competitive advantages are strong.' },
      ].map(step => (
        <div class="bg-surface-container-lowest p-8 border border-outline-variant/10">
          <span class="material-symbols-outlined text-tertiary-fixed-dim text-3xl mb-4 block">{step.icon}</span>
          <h3 class="font-headline text-xl text-primary-container mb-3">{step.title}</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-on-surface-variant leading-relaxed">{step.desc}</p>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Key Characteristics -->
  <section class="mb-16 bg-primary-container text-surface px-8 md:px-12 py-12 relative overflow-hidden">
    <div class="absolute top-0 right-0 w-64 h-64 bg-secondary/10 rounded-full blur-3xl translate-x-1/3 -translate-y-1/3 pointer-events-none"></div>
    <h2 class="font-headline text-3xl text-tertiary-fixed mb-10 relative z-10">Key <span class="italic">Characteristics at a Glance</span></h2>
    <div class="grid grid-cols-2 md:grid-cols-3 lg:grid-cols-4 gap-4 relative z-10">
      {[
        { label: 'Minimum Corpus',       value: '₹20 Crore',        sub: 'per scheme' },
        { label: 'Min. Investor Ticket', value: '₹1 Crore',         sub: '₹25L for employees' },
        { label: 'Fund Structure',       value: 'Close-Ended',       sub: 'mandatory' },
        { label: 'Typical Tenure',       value: '5–7 Years',         sub: 'incl. extension options' },
        { label: 'Leverage',             value: 'Not Permitted',     sub: 'except short-term borrowing' },
        { label: 'Taxation',             value: 'Pass-Through',      sub: 'Sec. 224, IT Act 2025' },
        { label: 'Target IRR',           value: '18–25%',            sub: 'gross, indicative' },
        { label: 'Ticket Size',          value: '₹2–20 Crore',      sub: 'per investee company' },
      ].map(p => (
        <div class="border border-secondary/30 p-5">
          <p class="text-[10px] uppercase font-label tracking-wider text-slate-400 mb-1">{p.label}</p>
          <p class="font-headline text-xl text-tertiary-fixed leading-tight">{p.value}</p>
          <p class="text-[10px] text-slate-500 mt-1">{p.sub}</p>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Risk Factors -->
  <section class="mb-16">
    <h2 class="font-headline text-4xl text-primary-container mb-6">Risk Considerations</h2>
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
      {[
        { icon: 'person', title: 'Promoter / Key-Person Risk', desc: 'SMEs are often founder-dependent. The success of the investment is heavily tied to the promoter\'s vision, capacity, and willingness to share control with an institutional investor.' },
        { icon: 'lock', title: 'Exit Uncertainty', desc: 'SME platform listing requires minimum revenue and profitability thresholds that investees may not meet within the fund tenure. Strategic sale timelines are similarly unpredictable.' },
        { icon: 'account_balance', title: 'Governance & Compliance Risk', desc: 'Many SMEs have informal accounting, undeclared cash transactions, or weak legal documentation. Due diligence must address these before investment, and remediation post-investment is complex.' },
        { icon: 'trending_down', title: 'Economic Cycle Sensitivity', desc: 'SMEs are more vulnerable to macro shocks — GST changes, raw material price inflation, export demand disruptions — than large-caps. Portfolio companies may face cash flow stress in downturns.' },
      ].map(r => (
        <div class="bg-surface-container-lowest p-8 border border-outline-variant/10 flex gap-4">
          <span class="material-symbols-outlined text-secondary text-2xl shrink-0 mt-0.5">{r.icon}</span>
          <div>
            <h3 class="font-semibold text-primary-container mb-2">{r.title}</h3>
            <p class="text-sm text-on-surface-variant leading-relaxed">{r.desc}</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- CTA -->
  <section class="bg-primary-container text-white px-10 md:px-16 py-12 flex flex-col md:flex-row items-start md:items-center justify-between gap-8 relative overflow-hidden mb-12">
    <div class="absolute top-0 right-0 w-64 h-64 bg-secondary/10 rounded-full blur-3xl translate-x-1/3 -translate-y-1/3 pointer-events-none"></div>
    <div class="max-w-lg relative z-10">
      <h2 class="font-headline text-3xl text-amber-100 mb-2">Explore SME Fund Opportunities</h2>
      <p class="text-slate-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">Access SEBI-registered SME AIFs through Platizio Alternatives's institutional investment platform.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-4 relative z-10">
      <a href="/explore" class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 bg-tertiary-fixed text-on-tertiary-fixed px-8 py-4 text-[11px] uppercase font-bold tracking-widest hover:opacity-90 transition-opacity">
        Browse Funds <span class="material-symbols-outlined text-sm">arrow_forward</span>
      </a>
      <button type="button" class="js-open-consult inline-flex items-center gap-2 border border-white/30 text-white px-8 py-4 text-[11px] uppercase font-bold tracking-widest hover:bg-white/10 transition-colors cursor-pointer">
        Speak to Advisor
      </button>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Prev / Next -->
  <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-4">
    <a href="/knowledge/aif/category-i/social-venture" class="flex-1 border border-outline p-5 hover:border-secondary transition-colors group text-center">
      <span class="text-[10px] uppercase tracking-widest text-outline block mb-1">Previous</span>
      <span class="font-headline text-lg text-primary-container group-hover:text-secondary transition-colors">Social Venture Funds</span>
    </a>
    <a href="/knowledge/aif/category-ii" class="flex-1 border border-outline p-5 hover:border-secondary transition-colors group text-center">
      <span class="text-[10px] uppercase tracking-widest text-outline block mb-1">Next</span>
      <span class="font-headline text-lg text-primary-container group-hover:text-secondary transition-colors">Category II AIF</span>
    </a>
  </div>

</div>
</BaseLayout>
